// Cross-version fixture corpus for AlternateMetadata.
//
// These are NOT hand-written byte arrays.  Each blob was produced by the
// serializer as it actually shipped at that version: the historical
// alternate_metadata.{h,cc} and content_type.h were checked out at a commit at
// which the shipped serializer was that version, compiled standalone against a
// generator that fills one fixed field vector, and the emitted bytes pasted
// here verbatim.  A hand-transcribed fixture only proves that the reader agrees
// with whoever transcribed it; this corpus proves it agrees with what was
// written to real volumes.
//
// Producing commits (the optimizer repository).  v4-v7 are the version-bump
// commits themselves (parent -> commit crosses the version).  The v3 row is
// NOT a bump commit and is not claimed to be one: it is simply a commit whose
// tree carries the shipped v3 serializer, chosen because it is reachable.
//   v3  6ea16c2bd73de3903c7d3f7f70204f8cfd877950  (tree at kCurrentVersion = 3)
//   v4  dd00db5db35899cf8f147f388ea03319a7e33738  3 -> 4
//   v5  fd5a1e13777a5fde896c9406bdb7026eb343be72  4 -> 5
//   v6  9697a8cbb79ac96c876beee0919f8078e15e4d1c  5 -> 6
//   v7  48c4dca84dc8fa032e482ef05ed5194036fe41c3  6 -> 7
//
// REGENERATION NEEDS FULL HISTORY.  These commits are older than a shallow
// clone reaches, so `git show <sha>:lib/classify/alternate_metadata.cc` fails
// with "invalid object name" in a default CI checkout.  Fetch full history
// before regenerating.  A regeneration instruction that cannot be followed is
// a corpus that quietly becomes hand-maintained, which is the one thing this
// file exists not to be.
//
// Two vectors per version:
//   *Full     — every field the version has, populated with distinguishable
//               values, including a flags byte with an UNASSIGNED bit set
//               (0x81) so the corpus also pins the "unknown flag bits survive"
//               contract.
//   *Minimal  — struct defaults: empty content-type, empty ETag, zeros.  This
//               is the shortest blob each version can produce.
//
// The shared field vector (fields absent from a version are simply not set):
//   full_mask 0x1234ABCD, content_type kImage, flags 0x81,
//   origin_content_type "image/jpeg", cache_inserted_at 1700000000,
//   origin_max_age 3600, origin_s_maxage 7200, origin_cc_flags 0x0355,
//   ssimulacra2_score_x100 9012, content_class 1,
//   origin_last_modified 1699999000, origin_etag "\"abc-123\"",
//   origin_content_length 123456,
//   origin_html_hash bytes 0x01..0x20, render_source_hash bytes 0xF0..0xD1.
//
// To regenerate, see the header comment of the test that consumes this file.

